IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII, "Sureties to Keep the Peace": section 810 (the general peace bond:
-- fear of injury, damage or an offence under section 162.1), section 810.01 (fear of a section 423.1 or criminal organization offence)
-- and section 810.011 (fear of a terrorism offence). Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a
-- converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE OF A PEACE-BOND SECTION. Each section has the same bones, and each bone is a function of its own:
--   who may lay an information; the judge's duty to cause the parties to appear; the power to order a recognizance (an "If ... satisfied" gate);
--   the longest period; the power to commit on refusal; the conditions the judge may add; the duty to consider a firearms prohibition and,
--   if it is desirable, to add it, to specify its surrender, and to state reasons if not; variance; and the sections that apply.
-- A "may" function answers NOTHING when an "if" gate fails (the 2026-11-12 ruling); a "Where / on application / before" gate answers JUST FALSE
-- and is listed in NOTES.md for a lawyer; a duty whose opening fails answers JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a)); a stated maximum period or term
-- beyond its limit answers JUST FALSE ("not more than").

§ `Section 810 -- Sureties to keep the peace: fear of injury, damage or an offence under section 162.1`

-- 810(1) An information may be laid before a justice by or on behalf of any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person (a) will cause personal injury ... or will damage their property; or (b) will commit an offence under section 162.1.
-- src:16830 | If injury or damage feared
-- src:16831 | 810 (1) An information may be laid before a justice by or on behalf of any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person
-- src:16832 | (a) will cause personal injury to them or to their intimate partner or child or will damage their property; or
-- src:16833 | (b) will commit an offence under section 162.1.
@ref Criminal Code s 810(1) to s 810(1)(b) (src:16830-16833)
DECLARE `s 810(1) feared event` IS ONE OF
    `s 810(1)(a) personal injury to the person or to their intimate partner or child, or damage to their property`
    `s 810(1)(b) an offence under section 162.1`
    `s 810(1) another feared event`

@ref Criminal Code s 810(1) (src:16830-16831)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate "any person who fears on reasonable grounds" (fork F-810-1)
GIVEN `the information is laid by or on behalf of a person who fears on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      event IS A `s 810(1) feared event`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810(1) an information may be laid before a justice` MEANS
    IF `the information is laid by or on behalf of a person who fears on reasonable grounds`
    THEN CONSIDER event
         WHEN `s 810(1)(a) personal injury to the person or to their intimate partner or child, or damage to their property` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810(1)(b) an offence under section 162.1` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810(1) another feared event` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) will cause personal injury ... or (b) will commit an offence under section 162.1"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who fears on reasonable grounds"

-- 810(2) A justice who receives an information under subsection (1) shall cause the parties to appear before him or before a summary conviction court having jurisdiction in the same territorial division.
-- src:16834 | Duty of justice
-- src:16835 | (2) A justice who receives an information under subsection (1) shall cause the parties to appear before him or before a summary conviction court having jurisdiction in the same territorial division.
@ref Criminal Code s 810(2) (src:16834-16835)
GIVEN `the justice receives an information under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810(2) the justice is required to cause the parties to appear` MEANS
    IF `the justice receives an information under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A justice who receives an information under subsection (1)"

DECLARE `s 810 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810(2) cause the parties to appear`
    `s 810(3.1) consider the firearms condition`
    `s 810(3.1) add the firearms condition`
    `s 810(3.11) specify the manner of surrender`
    `s 810(3.12) include a statement of reasons in the record`
    `s 810(3.2) consider the supplementary conditions`

@ref Criminal Code s 810(2) (src:16834-16835)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810 action`
`s 810(2) the justice is to cause the parties to appear` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810(2) cause the parties to appear`

-- 810(3) If the justice or summary conviction court ... is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the person on whose behalf the information was laid has reasonable grounds for the fear, the justice or court may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties, to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period of not more than 12 months.
