-- 810(3.02) The justice or summary conviction court may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions that require the defendant (a) to abstain from the consumption of drugs ..., alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; (b) to provide ... a sample of a bodily substance ... on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated ...; or (c) to provide ... a sample ... at regular intervals ... specified, in a notice in Form 51 ...
-- src:16840 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:16841 | (3.02) The justice or summary conviction court may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the justice or court considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant, including conditions that require the defendant
-- src:16842 | (a) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:16843 | (b) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(a) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the defendant has breached a condition of the recognizance that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; or
-- src:16844 | (c) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified, in a notice in Form 51 served on the defendant, by a probation officer or a person designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(b) to specify them, if a condition of the recognizance requires the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810(3.02) to s 810(3.02)(c) (src:16840-16844)
DECLARE `s 810(3.02) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810(3.02)(a) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 810(3.02)(b) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 810(3.02)(c) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 810(3.02) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810(3.02) (src:16840-16841)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the justice or court considers desirable"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810(3.02) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or court considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the justice or court considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810(3.02)(a) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810(3.02)(b) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810(3.02)(c) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810(3.02) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions ... that the justice or court considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"

-- 810(3.1) Before making an order under subsection (3), the justice or the summary conviction court shall consider whether it is desirable ... to include as a condition ... that the defendant be prohibited from possessing any firearm ... and, if the justice or summary conviction court decides that it is so desirable, ... shall add such a condition.
