§ `Section 810.01 -- Fear of an offence under section 423.1 or a criminal organization offence`

-- 810.01(1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 423.1 or a criminal organization offence may, with the Attorney General's consent, lay an information before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16863 | Fear of certain offences
-- src:16864 | 810.01 (1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 423.1 or a criminal organization offence may, with the Attorney General’s consent, lay an information before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(1) (src:16863-16864)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate and "with the Attorney General's consent" (fork F-810.01-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 423.1 or a criminal organization offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 423.1 or a criminal organization offence` AND `the Attorney General consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fears on reasonable grounds ... may, with the Attorney General's consent, lay an information"

-- 810.01(2) A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16865 | Appearances
