    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a term not exceeding twelve months"

-- 810.01(4.1) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions that require the defendant (a) to participate in a treatment program; (b) to wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request; (c) to remain within a specified geographic area ...; (d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times; (e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs ...; (f) to provide ... a sample ... on demand ...; or (g) to provide ... a sample ... at regular intervals ... Form 51.
-- src:16873 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:16874 | (4.1) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable for preventing the commission of an offence referred to in subsection (1), including conditions that require the defendant
-- src:16875 | (a) to participate in a treatment program;
-- src:16876 | (b) to wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request;
-- src:16877 | (c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the judge;
-- src:16878 | (d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times;
-- src:16879 | (e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs, except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:16880 | (f) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(a) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the defendant has breached a condition of the recognizance that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; or
-- src:16881 | (g) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified, in a notice in Form 51 served on the defendant, by a probation officer or a person designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(b) to specify them, if a condition of the recognizance requires the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(4.1) to s 810.01(4.1)(g) (src:16873-16881)
DECLARE `s 810.01(4.1) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.01(4.1)(a) to participate in a treatment program`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the judge`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 810.01(4.1)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 810.01(4.1) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(4.1) (src:16873-16874)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the judge considers desirable for preventing the commission of an offence"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810.01(4.1) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the condition desirable for preventing the commission of an offence referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the judge considers the condition desirable for preventing the commission of an offence referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(a) to participate in a treatment program` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` THEN IF `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General makes the request"
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the judge` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(4.1) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable for preventing the commission of an offence"

-- 810.01(5) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable ... to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
-- src:16882 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:16883 | (5) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the defendant’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(5) (src:16882-16883)
