GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under section 810.01 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provincial court judge shall consider" in proceedings under this section

@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(5) (src:16882-16883)
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so"

DECLARE `s 810.01 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.01(5) consider the firearms condition`
    `s 810.01(5) add the firearms condition and specify the period`
    `s 810.01(5.1) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered`
    `s 810.01(5.2) include a statement of reasons in the record`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(5) (src:16882-16883)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.01 action`
`s 810.01(5) the judge is to consider the firearms condition` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.01(5) consider the firearms condition`
    HENCE `s 810.01(5) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(5) (src:16882-16883)
