      `the Attorney General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(6) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the informant applies` OR `the Attorney General applies` OR `the defendant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the informant, the Attorney General or the defendant"

