    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to recognizances made under this section"

-- 810.01(8) With respect to proceedings under this section, Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes the lawful deputy of any of them.
-- src:16892 | Definition of Attorney General
-- src:16893 | (8) With respect to proceedings under this section, Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes the lawful deputy of any of them.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(8) "Attorney General" (src:16892-16893)
DECLARE `s 810.01(8) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of Canada`
    `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken`
    `s 810.01(8) the lawful deputy of one of them`
    `s 810.01(8) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.01(8) "Attorney General" (src:16892-16893)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.01` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 810.01(8) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.01(8) Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.01`
    THEN CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(8) the lawful deputy of one of them` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.01(8) another person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to proceedings under this section"

§ `Section 810.011 -- Fear of a terrorism offence`

-- 810.011(1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person may commit a terrorism offence may, with the Attorney General's consent, lay an information before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16894 | Fear of terrorism offence
-- src:16895 | 810.011 (1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person may commit a terrorism offence may, with the Attorney General’s consent, lay an information before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(1) (src:16894-16895)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate and "with the Attorney General's consent" (fork F-810.011-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person may commit a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.011(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person may commit a terrorism offence` AND `the Attorney General consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fears on reasonable grounds ... may, with the Attorney General's consent, lay an information"

-- 810.011(2) The provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
