         WHEN `s 810.011(6) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"

-- 810.011(7) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable ... to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which it applies.
-- src:16912 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:16913 | (7) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the defendant’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which it applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(7) (src:16912-16913)
GIVEN `the information was laid under section 810.011 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
