-- 810.011(10) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, to secure the good conduct of the defendant, to include in the recognizance a condition that the defendant remain within a specified geographic area ... If the judge decides that it is desirable, the judge shall add the condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which it applies.
