-- 810.011(14) With respect to proceedings under this section, Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes the lawful deputy of any of them.
-- src:16926 | Definition of Attorney General
-- src:16927 | (14) With respect to proceedings under this section, Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province in which those proceedings are taken and includes the lawful deputy of any of them.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(14) "Attorney General" (src:16926-16927)
DECLARE `s 810.011(14) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of Canada`
    `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken`
    `s 810.011(14) the lawful deputy of one of them`
    `s 810.011(14) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(14) "Attorney General" (src:16926-16927)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.011` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 810.011(14) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.011(14) Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.011`
    THEN CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.011(14) the lawful deputy of one of them` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.011(14) another person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Attorney General means either the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of the province"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to proceedings under this section"

-- 810.011(15) Each year, the Attorney General of Canada shall prepare and cause to be laid before each House of Parliament a report setting out the number of recognizances entered into under this section in the previous year.
-- src:16928 | Annual report
-- src:16929 | (15) Each year, the Attorney General of Canada shall prepare and cause to be laid before each House of Parliament a report setting out the number of recognizances entered into under this section in the previous year.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(15) (src:16928-16929)
-- @fork F-810.011-15: "Each year" says how often, not by when; no deadline, consequence or sitting-day rule is stated, so none is encoded.
DECLARE `s 810.011 report action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.011(15) prepare the annual report and cause it to be laid before each House of Parliament`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.011(15) (src:16928-16929)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.011 report action`
`s 810.011(15) the Attorney General of Canada is to prepare and lay the annual report` MEANS
    PARTY `the Attorney General of Canada`
    MUST `s 810.011(15) prepare the annual report and cause it to be laid before each House of Parliament`
